      "defect": "overstrong-title-or-statement",
      "evidence": "The item calls the countable-partition definition “genuinely stronger,” but the two suprema always agree. For any countable partition E=⨆E_n, the finite partition E_0,...,E_N,⋃_{n>N}E_n has sum at least Σ_{n=0}^N|ν(E_n)|. Letting N tend to infinity shows the finite-partition supremum is at least that countable partition's sum; the reverse inequality is immediate because finite partitions are countable. Steps 1.1–2.1 establish only nonattainment by finite partitions, not a larger countable-partition supremum.",
